<title>LATVIA: LATVIA-TWO T-BILL YIELDS DOWN, ONE UP, ONE STABLE.</title>
<headline>LATVIA-TWO T-BILL YIELDS DOWN, ONE UP, ONE STABLE.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield of six-month</p>
<p>Latvian T-bills was the only one to rise at auction on</p>
<p>Wednesday, but three-month and twelve-month papers saw a rise</p>
<p>in yield, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>One year paper was last auctioned on January 29. The 28-day</p>
<p>paper yield remained stable.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of lats.</p>
<p> MATURITY  AV YLD(pct) LAST WEEK NO OF BANKS ISSUE  BID   SOLD</p>
<p> One month    3.70	  3.70	 3	  0.50  1.10  0.50</p>
<p> Three-month  5.73	  5.74	 3	  1.00  1.36  0.36</p>
<p> Six-month    6.17	  5.63	 6	  1.50  3.40  1.50</p>
<p> Twelve-month 8.20	  8.21	11	 12.00 24.27 12.00</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
